    "q-96955": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.01.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.3263)=0.99.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.3263)=1-0.99=0.01.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.3263)=0.01.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270828/assets/2212ee9de7a440c5d61814d1b2b50a249849756a4aa331e4f48180c67f95944f.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.3263) & =0.01 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.3263) & =0.01.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.3263.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
