    "q-47501": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 26",
      "problem": "Anna decides to go jogging. Her position from the starting point, measured in meters, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $14$ | $25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=7$ using a central difference approximation with the step size $h=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=7$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(7) & ≈\\frac{s(7+2)-s(7-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(9)-s(5)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{14-4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the velocity of Anna at the instant of time $t=7$ is $2.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
