    "q-37920": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 33",
      "problem": "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5z-4y+2x \\\\ 3y-2z+6x \\\\ 4z-8x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+5z \\\\ 6x+3y-2z \\\\ -8x-y+4z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $3\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+5z \\\\ 6x+3y-2z \\\\ -8x-y+4z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+5z \\\\ 6x+3y-2z \\\\ -8x-y+4z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Hence, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-37920-a",
